Here's how to handle each scenario with modern MSTest (3.9+/3.10+):

## 1. Windows-only (registry tests)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]
public void Registry_ReadsExpectedValue()
{
    var value = Registry.GetValue(@"HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\...", "Key", null);
    Assert.IsNotNull(value);
}
```

## 2. Skip in CI (requires local GPU)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[CICondition(ConditionMode.Exclude)]
public void RenderFrame_ProducesExpectedOutput()
{
    var frame = _gpuRenderer.Render(scene);
    Assert.IsNotNull(frame);
}
```

## 3. Flaky external API (retry)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)]
[Timeout(10000)]
public async Task GetWeather_ReturnsForecast(TestContext testContext)
{
    var forecast = await _weatherClient.GetForecastAsync(testContext.CancellationToken);
    Assert.IsNotNull(forecast);
}
```

Use `[Retry(N)]` only for genuinely flaky external dependencies — not to mask race conditions.

## 4. Cleanup temp files even on failure

Use `[TestCleanup]` — it runs regardless of test outcome:

```csharp
[TestClass]
public sealed class FileProcessorTests
{
    private string _tempFile = string.Empty;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessFile_WritesExpectedContent()
    {
        FileProcessor.Process(_tempFile);
        var content = File.ReadAllText(_tempFile);
        Assert.Contains("expected", content);
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        if (File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }
}
```

### Combining them

You can stack attributes freely:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]
[CICondition(ConditionMode.Exclude)]
[Retry(2)]
[Timeout(15000)]
public async Task FullIntegration_WindowsGpuWeather(TestContext testContext) { ... }
```

**Minimum versions:** `[Retry]` requires MSTest 3.9+, `[OSCondition]`/`[CICondition]` require MSTest 3.10+.
